Bugfix: "Request again" sends the reset mail after a failed attempt

When the password reset mail could not be sent, the token of the failed attempt
stayed stored. "Request again" within the next five minutes then counted as a
repeated request: no mail was sent, but the page reported success. A failed
mail now removes its token, so the next request sends the mail again. The
answer for unknown users and the five minute limit after a mail that went out
are unchanged.
